{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TwoOperatorResidualSplit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TwoOperatorResidualSplit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanThreeBodyCluster","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.Mu4RhoFCluster","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.HeliumFourBodyCluster"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.residual_is_two_operator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.residual_is_two_operator","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L194-L234","doc":"**(CAPSTONE) The Δ_λ residual is a TWO-operator (binding − saturation)\nobject.**  Model the A=3 moment `μ₃ > 0` and the A=4 moment `μ₄ = mu4Residual`\neach as a signed split (`hmodel`).  Then, purely from the proved sign structure:\n\n1. **A=3 is binding-dominated** — `μ₃ > 0` forces the binding value above the\n   saturation magnitude (`S₃ < B₃`), so the positive odd moment is carried by the\n   non-negative Brunnian/Borromean operator (`borromean_cluster_nonneg`, #4360).\n2. **A=4 is saturation-dominated** — `μ₄ < 0` (`mu4Residual_neg`, #4376) forces\n   the saturation magnitude above the binding value (`B₄ < S₄`), so the negative\n   even moment is carried by the non-positive multiplicative operator\n   (`pairwise_3body_content_nonpos`, #4354).\n3. **Two operators of opposite sign are necessary** — no single-sign model spans\n   both: a binding-only (`S = 0`, hence `≥ 0`) split can never equal `μ₄ < 0`,\n   and a saturation-only (`B = 0`, hence `≤ 0`) split can never equal `μ₃ > 0`.\n\nThe sign pattern (`μ₃ > 0` selects binding, `μ₄ < 0` selects saturation) is\nexactly what the two proved cluster-sign lemmas force.  This is the structural\n`sign_swap_a3_a4` (#4376) read as a *decomposition*: the residual is neither the\nbinding operator alone nor the saturation operator alone, but their signed\ndifference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.signed_split_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.signed_split_exists","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L180-L190","doc":"**Every real moment admits *some* signed split.**  This is the *weak* form —\nit says nothing about the physical operator magnitudes; it merely records that\n`μ = B − S` with `B, S ≥ 0` is always solvable (`B = max μ 0`, `S = max (−μ) 0`).\nThe STRONG form — that the concrete Borromean binding and multiplicative\nsaturation magnitudes sum to the exact AME `μₖ` — is the OPEN Δ_λ magnitude\nclosure and is deliberately NOT proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4MinusSaturation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4MinusSaturation","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L166-L176","doc":"The A=4 binding half of the split, built from the merged\n`brunnian4Cluster_nonneg` (#4376): `B = brunnian4Cluster E₀ τ h ≥ 0` whenever the\nlevel trace lies at or below the unlink (`τ h ≤ 1`), paired with any non-negative\nsaturation magnitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.borromeanMinusSaturation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.borromeanMinusSaturation","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L150-L164","doc":"**The concrete two-operator split** built entirely from the proved sign\nlemmas: the binding value `B = E₀·(1 − τ_Borr)` is non-negative by the merged\n`borromean_cluster_nonneg` (#4360); the saturation magnitude\n`S = saturationMagnitude f_a f_b f_c` is non-negative by\n`saturationMagnitude_nonneg` (which reuses `pairwise_3body_content_nonpos`,\n#4354).  This exhibits `B − S` as a genuine binding-minus-saturation object with\nBOTH signs derived — not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.saturationMagnitude_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.saturationMagnitude_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L141-L148","doc":"**The saturation magnitude is non-negative** — a direct reuse of the merged\nsign wall `pairwise_3body_content_nonpos` (#4354): the multiplicative cluster\ncontent `f_a + f_b + f_c − f_a f_b f_c − 2 ≤ 0`, so its negative is `≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.saturationMagnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.saturationMagnitude","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L136-L139","doc":"The **saturation magnitude** of the multiplicative 3-body interface product:\n`S = 2 − f_a − f_b − f_c + f_a f_b f_c = −(f_a + f_b + f_c − f_a f_b f_c − 2)`,\ni.e. minus the (`≤ 0`) beyond-pairwise cluster content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.saturation_alone_ne_mu3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.saturation_alone_ne_mu3","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L125-L132","doc":"**A saturation-only model cannot reach `μ₃ > 0`.**  A pure-saturation residual\nis `≤ 0` (`pure_saturation_nonpos`), but `μ₃ = +0.4708 > 0`.  So no `B = 0` split\nequals `μ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.binding_alone_ne_mu4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.binding_alone_ne_mu4","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L116-L123","doc":"**A binding-only model cannot reach `μ₄`.**  `μ₄ = −4.591 < 0`\n(`mu4Residual_neg`, #4376), but a pure-binding residual is `≥ 0`\n(`pure_binding_nonneg`).  So no `S = 0` split equals `μ₄`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.pure_saturation_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.pure_saturation_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L107-L112","doc":"**Pure saturation is non-positive.**  If the binding operator is switched off\n(`B = 0`), the residual is `−S ≤ 0`.  A single non-positive operator can never\nrealize a positive moment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.pure_binding_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.pure_binding_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L100-L105","doc":"**Pure binding is non-negative.**  If the saturation operator is switched off\n(`S = 0`), the residual is just the binding value `B ≥ 0`, hence `≥ 0`.  A\nsingle non-negative operator can never realize a negative moment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.residual_neg_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.residual_neg_iff","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L94-L96","doc":"**Saturation-dominated ⟺ negative residual.**  `μ = B − S < 0 ↔ B < S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.residual_pos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.residual_pos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L90-L92","doc":"**Binding-dominated ⟺ positive residual.**  `μ = B − S > 0 ↔ S < B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.residual","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L85-L86","doc":"The realized residual moment `μ = B − S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.hS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.hS","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.hB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.hB","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.S","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Saturation magnitude (`= −` multiplicative cluster); non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.B","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Binding contribution (Brunnian/Borromean deficit); non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SignedResidualSplit","kind":"structure","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TwoOperatorResidualSplit.lean#L72-L83","doc":"A **two-operator residual split**: a residual moment realized as\n`residual = B − S`, where `B ≥ 0` is a *binding* contribution (a Brunnian trace\ndeficit, provably non-negative) and `S ≥ 0` is a *saturation* magnitude (the\nnegative of a provably non-positive multiplicative cluster).  The two operators\nhave opposite sign by construction — that is the whole content. ","signatureChunk":0}]}